    <h2 id="industry-context">Real-World Industry Context: Why Aerosol Hair Products Require Specialized Expertise</h2>
    <p>Cosmetic aerosol hair products are not generic cosmetic items—they are pressurized engineered systems that combine formulation chemistry, mechanical hardware, and regulatory compliance. Unlike conventional hair products, aerosol failures can lead to spray inconsistency, clogging, pressure loss, corrosion, or safety recalls if not properly engineered.</p>
    <p>In professional practice, most performance issues in hair spray formulations, temporary hair colour formulations, or aerosol shampoo systems originate not from ingredients alone, but from misalignment between chemistry, propellant behavior, and aerosol hardware. This makes aerosol hair products a highly specialized domain requiring cross-disciplinary expertise rather than trial-and-error development.</p>

