    <h2 id="chemistry-ecosystem">Aerosol Chemistry Ecosystem in Hair Products</h2>
    <p>While formulations are proprietary, the chemistry ecosystem behind cosmetic aerosol hair products is well-established and regulated. These systems involve a structured interaction between film-forming polymers, solvents, conditioning agents, pigments or absorbents, and propellants, all engineered for stability and safety.</p>
    <p>Compatibility between formulation components and aerosol hardware is critical. Instability can lead to clogging, pressure loss, inconsistent spray, or product separation over shelf life.</p>

